id #edb/ref 17592186711330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a7971f0-8a06-58fc-b744-54a3be1566cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711330} :answer-field/id #uuid "6127c587-3280-53f6-a4a7-48113f5222d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0c849949-437e-5c00-9474-96f0d9a4793c" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(14,4)$ for the curve $\\sqrt{y} + \\sqrt{x + 2}=6$.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate the square roots using the power and chain rules.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\sqrt{y} + \\sqrt{x + 2}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(6\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\frac{dy}{dx}}{2 \\sqrt{y}} + \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x + 2}}&=0\\\\\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x + 2}}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x + 2}}}{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(14,4)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $\\frac{1}{4}\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(14,4)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}}{\\frac{1}{4}}\\\\\n&=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8866afd0-edf1-5716-bdf7-bea245d742c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8866afd0-edf1-5716-bdf7-bea245d742c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711332} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8cf838-4eb2-554c-85b4-87c265de44cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2410ab30-fefe-5216-8520-85aaeaba5c2e" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(11,16)$ for the curve $\\sqrt{y} + \\sqrt{x - 2}=7$.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate the square roots using the power and chain rules.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\sqrt{y} + \\sqrt{x - 2}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(7\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{\\frac{dy}{dx}}{2 \\sqrt{y}} + \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x - 2}}&=0\\\\\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x - 2}}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x - 2}}}{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(11,16)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $\\frac{1}{8}\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(11,16)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{6}}{\\frac{1}{8}}\\\\\n&=- \\frac{4}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a73a181-a848-569c-a622-74cdad86fad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711321} {:answer/id #uuid "afaff60d-0c88-58d0-90d2-f96b5c4da5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711335} {:answer/id #uuid "ead10aa1-0e06-5bfc-82de-1f57e77729f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711340} {:answer/id #uuid "eb27843d-1eff-5a8e-a353-18caab0c17c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711341} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2107fb-8e2c-532b-9d6e-53cbf53d05f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb27843d-1eff-5a8e-a353-18caab0c17c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711341} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fca0757-d32b-51fb-967f-c1396cb9c016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "325ff2e4-ed82-59d7-8afd-e09d94d4b8e3" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)$ for the curve $y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Use the product rule on the cosine product; the derivative of $\\cos(x)$ is $-\\sin(x)$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}&=0\\\\\n\\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(- y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{- y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(- \\frac{\\pi}{6},1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\\\\n&=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e7f24fd-d0e5-55cb-af43-ec9310b2c1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e7f24fd-d0e5-55cb-af43-ec9310b2c1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711333} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d2da5e-c7a8-5e0c-b08e-af350752290e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b079871a-abab-5663-a7d0-bbddd1029f40" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(-2,1)$ for the curve $x^{2} y + x=2$.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Use the product rule on the mixed power term and the chain rule on powers of $y$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{2} y + x\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} x^{2} + 2 x y + 1&=0\\\\\n\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(2 x y + 1\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{2 x y + 1}{x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-2,1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $4\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-2,1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{-3}{4}\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23a313fb-d091-5944-a80a-6adbb2b4552e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711322} {:answer/id #uuid "2483a172-3269-5e8c-8164-f6d231544d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711324} {:answer/id #uuid "55e94563-b149-51bf-926b-0a7a3306a775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711327} {:answer/id #uuid "775374bf-9805-5040-98ce-7df75bb14096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711329} {:answer/id #uuid "daf603b7-2c8c-5294-84c9-fb563852ea1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "775374bf-9805-5040-98ce-7df75bb14096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711329} :answer-field/id #uuid "a471d3c7-c0fc-50e9-9dac-8051cc285bb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c04e75a4-b35c-51fd-a0e8-6f7a3e694d0a" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(-2,0)$ for the curve $2 x^{2} - 2 x y - 2 y^{2}=8$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Use the product rule on $xy$ and the chain rule on powers of $y$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(2 x^{2} - 2 x y - 2 y^{2}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(8\\right)\\\\\n- 2 \\frac{dy}{dx} x - 4 \\frac{dy}{dx} y + 4 x - 2 y&=0\\\\\n\\left(- 2 x - 4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(4 x - 2 y\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{4 x - 2 y}{- 2 x - 4 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-2,0)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $4\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-2,0)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{-8}{4}\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "087afa85-fdc6-534a-acdc-d1b5c6514f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711344} {:answer/id #uuid "4031e969-25fa-5596-a496-4806625b4205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- e^{y}}{x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711350} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f4bc44-4973-5d07-bc76-db96c0920e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711364} {:answer/id #uuid "c405eb86-4856-56cd-9215-b48698e8b424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711365} {:answer/id #uuid "cee0c1a0-979d-5b0e-9c06-db710304788b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "087afa85-fdc6-534a-acdc-d1b5c6514f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711344} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c1f0c8c-491d-525a-bca2-8c9af60115f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "41f890ee-0f40-5a78-8d02-0a9e1c7eda1f" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ for $2 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - y^{2}=- x e^{y}$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$ and write $y'=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$. Use the **product rule** for each mixed product, including the chain-rule factor $y^{\\prime}$ when differentiating a function of $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(2 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)&=- 2 x^{2} y' \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- x e^{y}\\right)&=- x y' e^{y} - e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the equation, collect all terms containing $y^{\\prime}$, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + y' \\left(- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 y\\right)&=- x y' e^{y}\\\\\n&\\quad -e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y\\right)y^{\\prime}&=- 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad -e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDivide by the coefficient of $y^{\\prime}$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{- 4 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - e^{y}}{- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies where $- 2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} - 2 y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e6441d-c364-5fb2-907d-a9f101c8bcc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{y}}{- x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711349} {:answer/id #uuid "644b1acb-5514-5e27-8e82-b31029e24219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711355} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecddf3e-8704-58e6-ba37-066019bbb243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711358} {:answer/id #uuid "9f9721d3-a4ac-5e60-a4d7-5482cbee4edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711363} {:answer/id #uuid "e43ac478-5162-5ffc-8e7d-f3ebabd367f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f9721d3-a4ac-5e60-a4d7-5482cbee4edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711363} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d52e4b-4b28-5d9e-bbd3-dd4a173d4d85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "79aaf810-809b-5709-8b47-d89a5ac8339d" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ for $3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 y^{2}=x e^{y}$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$ and write $y'=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$. Use the **product rule** for each mixed product, including the chain-rule factor $y^{\\prime}$ when differentiating a function of $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)&=- 3 x^{2} y' \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x e^{y}\\right)&=x y' e^{y} + e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the equation, collect all terms containing $y^{\\prime}$, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + y' \\left(- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 4 y\\right)&=x y' e^{y}\\\\\n&\\quad +e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y\\right)y^{\\prime}&=- 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad +e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDivide by the coefficient of $y^{\\prime}$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{- 6 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{y}}{- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies where $- 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - x e^{y} + 4 y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194acef1-0a0e-57e5-88a2-dee652a39e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y}}{x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711345} {:answer/id #uuid "31432dba-f440-5edf-a26f-421ec04bd55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y} + 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{- x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711348} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2e6ffe-70e7-530a-8fc9-108cfc6199b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y}}{x^{2} e^{y} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711356} {:answer/id #uuid "dddc7d79-3a4b-5ac8-8447-018d0123125d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{x^{2} e^{y} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711367} {:answer/id #uuid "de0d19cc-68ef-585d-99ea-f166fc6c4a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de0d19cc-68ef-585d-99ea-f166fc6c4a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x e^{y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711368} :answer-field/id #uuid "43507860-08ac-53e8-8c30-a7f6d0024155" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9ec40e99-9c91-53b4-99f3-3d158efd6150" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ for $3 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} - 3 y^{2}=- x^{2} e^{y} - 2$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$ and write $y'=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$. Use the **product rule** for each mixed product, including the chain-rule factor $y^{\\prime}$ when differentiating a function of $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)&=3 x y' \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- x^{2} e^{y}\\right)&=- x^{2} y' e^{y} - 2 x e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the equation, collect all terms containing $y^{\\prime}$, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny' \\left(3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y\\right) + 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}&=- 2 x e^{y}\\\\\n&\\quad -x^{2} y' e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y\\right)y^{\\prime}&=- 2 x e^{y}\\\\\n&\\quad -3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDivide by the coefficient of $y^{\\prime}$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{- 2 x e^{y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}{x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies where $x^{2} e^{y} + 3 x \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 6 y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c01c04e-0381-53ed-a6b3-fe6950c01957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{- 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711346} {:answer/id #uuid "2a08935d-afa7-5b93-9bb7-fd0f99c63a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711347} {:answer/id #uuid "5342d7a6-40ba-5ba1-b390-5a9529b27b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711353} {:answer/id #uuid "8b113a3f-5cc4-565e-97e7-7328336400f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 e^{y}}{3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711359} {:answer/id #uuid "9aee0a3e-dd9b-5a36-a88c-0f5bc81c5115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{- 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a08935d-afa7-5b93-9bb7-fd0f99c63a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711347} :answer-field/id #uuid "608371e8-95e0-5c1f-8303-d2b1f9a7754c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e0ff24dd-1a2c-5f0f-9d68-cda7ba8fa221" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ for $3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 3 y^{2}=2 x e^{y} + 1$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$ and write $y'=\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$. Use the **product rule** for each mixed product, including the chain-rule factor $y^{\\prime}$ when differentiating a function of $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)&=3 x^{2} y' \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(2 x e^{y}\\right)&=2 x y' e^{y} + 2 e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the equation, collect all terms containing $y^{\\prime}$, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + y' \\left(3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} + 6 y\\right)&=2 x y' e^{y}\\\\\n&\\quad +2 e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y\\right)y^{\\prime}&=- 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\\\\n&\\quad +2 e^{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDivide by the coefficient of $y^{\\prime}$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{- 6 x \\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 e^{y}}{3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies where $3 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(y \\right)} - 2 x e^{y} + 6 y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6202a6d-edb1-5c45-9fef-ee613c52d7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-1} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6202a6d-edb1-5c45-9fef-ee613c52d7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-1} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711381} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8375ab7-5ae8-516a-a078-542398ef39f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "10853435-5cd6-5ae6-8d8b-65b2a158317c" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(1,-1)$ for the curve $- x^{2} + y e^{- x y}=- e - 1$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The outer product and the exponential chain rule both matter. First differentiate the exponential input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- x y\\right)&=- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(e^{- x y}\\right)&=\\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- x^{2} + y e^{- x y}\\right)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- e - 1\\right)\\\\\n&\\frac{dy}{dx} e^{- x y} - 2 x + y \\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}=0\\\\\n&\\left(- x y e^{- x y} + e^{- x y}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\left(- 2 x - y^{2} e^{- x y}\\right)\\\\\n&\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{- 2 x - y^{2} e^{- x y}}{- x y e^{- x y} + e^{- x y}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(1,-1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $2 e\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(1,-1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{- e - 2}{2 e}\\\\\n&=e^{-1} + \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98692f72-ffce-50b2-954b-8177a74db468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 e}{-2 + e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98692f72-ffce-50b2-954b-8177a74db468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 e}{-2 + e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711378} :answer-field/id #uuid "061b0482-b0dc-532b-a5dd-2fa98efc4cdc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2c7be21a-8842-5091-8749-22058da2baca" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(1,-1)$ for the curve $x e^{- x y} - y^{2}=-1 + e$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The outer product and the exponential chain rule both matter. First differentiate the exponential input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- x y\\right)&=- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(e^{- x y}\\right)&=\\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(x e^{- x y} - y^{2}\\right)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-1 + e\\right)\\\\\n&- 2 \\frac{dy}{dx} y + x \\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y} + e^{- x y}=0\\\\\n&\\left(- x^{2} e^{- x y} - 2 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\left(- x y e^{- x y} + e^{- x y}\\right)\\\\\n&\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{- x y e^{- x y} + e^{- x y}}{- x^{2} e^{- x y} - 2 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(1,-1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $2 - e\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(1,-1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{2 e}{2 - e}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 e}{-2 + e}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc339e5-3c4c-5b20-a5b4-fe2f74c687fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + e}{2 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc339e5-3c4c-5b20-a5b4-fe2f74c687fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + e}{2 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711377} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f58d016-d756-5628-b096-01b2e5ae5dd2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c16fc9a9-c3d5-57e3-a177-8d6900b45ab2" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(-1,1)$ for the curve $x^{2} + 2 y e^{- x y}=1 + 2 e$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The outer product and the exponential chain rule both matter. First differentiate the exponential input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- x y\\right)&=- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(e^{- x y}\\right)&=\\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{2} + 2 y e^{- x y}\\right)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(1 + 2 e\\right)\\\\\n&2 \\frac{dy}{dx} e^{- x y} + 2 x + 2 y \\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}=0\\\\\n&\\left(- 2 x y e^{- x y} + 2 e^{- x y}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\left(2 x - 2 y^{2} e^{- x y}\\right)\\\\\n&\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{2 x - 2 y^{2} e^{- x y}}{- 2 x y e^{- x y} + 2 e^{- x y}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-1,1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $4 e\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-1,1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{- 2 e - 2}{4 e}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1 + e}{2 e}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb2d236-fa4c-5a85-af88-58812c6f6cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb2d236-fa4c-5a85-af88-58812c6f6cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711373} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1deaae2-7326-5ad7-b5a4-fc6b01eae70b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d6912ccd-3ea1-50cd-97c0-026f7c889cf0" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(-1,-1)$ for the curve $- 2 x e^{- x y} + 2 y^{2}=\\frac{2}{e} + 2$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The outer product and the exponential chain rule both matter. First differentiate the exponential input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- x y\\right)&=- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(e^{- x y}\\right)&=\\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(- 2 x e^{- x y} + 2 y^{2}\\right)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{2}{e} + 2\\right)\\\\\n&4 \\frac{dy}{dx} y - 2 x \\left(- \\frac{dy}{dx} x - y\\right) e^{- x y} - 2 e^{- x y}=0\\\\\n&\\left(2 x^{2} e^{- x y} + 4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\left(2 x y e^{- x y} - 2 e^{- x y}\\right)\\\\\n&\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{2 x y e^{- x y} - 2 e^{- x y}}{2 x^{2} e^{- x y} + 4 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-1,-1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $-4 + \\frac{2}{e}\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-1,-1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{0}{-4 + \\frac{2}{e}}\\\\\n&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55096518-a771-56af-bf68-41a6c974dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711384} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7c8b1b-5049-5cf4-9493-df785a34d239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711389} {:answer/id #uuid "8796f00d-7296-5177-b298-ba16a18b0eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711391} {:answer/id #uuid "ae68fb96-2079-5e99-8c3d-227e4e5be525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711394} {:answer/id #uuid "caa5bf93-33da-5a8d-b378-3908e9525f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55096518-a771-56af-bf68-41a6c974dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711384} :answer-field/id #uuid "c521c3b1-5f5b-5396-8dbe-ea0268153e32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "572c159b-08a9-56eb-aac9-6f0ea7d93de3" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(-3,-3)$ for the curve $2 x^{3} - y^{3}=-27$." :question/worked-solution "Apply the power rule and the chain rule, treating $y$ as a function of $x$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(2 x^{3} - y^{3}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-27\\right)\\\\\n- 3 \\frac{dy}{dx} y^{2} + 6 x^{2}&=0\\\\\n\\left(- 3 y^{2}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(6 x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{6 x^{2}}{- 3 y^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-3,-3)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $-27\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-3,-3)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{54}{-27}\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c039f3d-d892-5139-b952-7944d6dea9a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711387} {:answer/id #uuid "72432db6-2bce-5aee-90df-6f5afaf418a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711388} {:answer/id #uuid "9a541242-84ea-58ef-923d-eaf65ca972f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711393} {:answer/id #uuid "c4991d51-fff6-56a9-b239-4f07665da572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711398} {:answer/id #uuid "f95a631e-2d1a-57a3-8d43-fa4f54f8d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72432db6-2bce-5aee-90df-6f5afaf418a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711388} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a23cb0-a764-5828-b907-c2eda93b22b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b6281bba-1242-5a1e-8367-b37608f41673" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(-1,1)$ for the curve $2 x^{3} - 3 y^{3}=-5$." :question/worked-solution "Apply the power rule and the chain rule, treating $y$ as a function of $x$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(2 x^{3} - 3 y^{3}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(-5\\right)\\\\\n- 9 \\frac{dy}{dx} y^{2} + 6 x^{2}&=0\\\\\n\\left(- 9 y^{2}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(6 x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{6 x^{2}}{- 9 y^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(-1,1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $-9\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(-1,1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{6}{-9}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55762c78-93fd-5f03-809b-41cf439ccc51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711385} {:answer/id #uuid "83cfb824-f3bf-5f7b-ab7b-1f64c27c35f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711390} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eceb5e-f417-522a-b16c-428c7e3f50a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711397} {:answer/id #uuid "efcddbc6-22b3-5ceb-b3a9-6a2f5e68badc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711401} {:answer/id #uuid "fed16c0f-d622-5ce9-af99-3250c0658c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83cfb824-f3bf-5f7b-ab7b-1f64c27c35f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711390} :answer-field/id #uuid "96179236-b608-5245-b09f-2e36b9f5c14a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b6d127f4-c50a-5474-9296-5d76423ad016" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,-1)$ for the curve $x^{3} - 3 y^{3}=4$." :question/worked-solution "Apply the power rule and the chain rule, treating $y$ as a function of $x$.\n\nDifferentiate both sides with respect to $x$, then collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{3} - 3 y^{3}\\right)&=\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(4\\right)\\\\\n- 9 \\frac{dy}{dx} y^{2} + 3 x^{2}&=0\\\\\n\\left(- 9 y^{2}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(3 x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{3 x^{2}}{- 9 y^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $(1,-1)$, the coefficient of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ is $-9\\ne 0$. Substitute the point to obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(1,-1)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{-9}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b812b7a-f863-5054-8492-311a8a7961d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{y + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711407} {:answer/id #uuid "45beb807-7bda-52bf-9cb9-741d62a85c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9 \\cot^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2 y - 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711408} {:answer/id #uuid "a98c1276-2ce2-5595-ac22-556b9ec85e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2 y + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711413} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bebd0a-2e14-5282-935e-3a9bd0f54761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{y + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711415} {:answer/id #uuid "ec21ad08-547d-597c-be5e-7659ef90edf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2 y + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec21ad08-547d-597c-be5e-7659ef90edf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2 y + 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711418} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5c9a17a-2cc1-5669-8066-d6ba20fdf3d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "11f9e0f9-a0e4-55ce-89f3-7d358939599d" :question/problem "Given that $y^{2} + 2 y-(3 \\tan{\\left(3 x \\right)})=0$, calculate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$. The chain rule gives $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(3 \\tan{\\left(3 x \\right)})=9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(y^{2} + 2 y\\right)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 \\tan{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n2 y\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollect the terms containing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(2 y + 2\\right)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{9 \\sec^{2}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{2 y + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies on real branches where $2 y + 2\\ne 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa6efae-5a9a-5e91-9229-682c2830321e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711406} {:answer/id #uuid "482f3672-d312-51b5-a445-07c4a1dcf8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711409} {:answer/id #uuid "6841b669-634d-530e-891f-18d8e2a1b3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711410} {:answer/id #uuid "8542bda8-00de-5781-9fad-439263aae18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711412} {:answer/id #uuid "d6786233-6656-501d-8f6a-b33040b20e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x^{2}}{3 y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8542bda8-00de-5781-9fad-439263aae18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711412} :answer-field/id #uuid "835ab5a6-e033-5aa0-a7e1-05a007edfd9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bcde03b1-e447-5561-bbbc-7df0d68680ed" :question/problem "Given that $y^{3} + \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}-(3 x^{2})=3$, calculate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$. Apply the chain rule to both functions of $y$, including the trigonometric derivative.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(y^{3} + \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3 x^{2} + 3\\right)\\\\\n3 y^{2}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+\\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=6 x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollect the terms containing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\right)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=6 x\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{6 x}{3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies on real branches where $3 y^{2} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}\\ne 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39e0a648-3847-5ccf-a8a2-075186f67b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711419} {:answer/id #uuid "3d32da3b-e5af-541a-8b34-af60b3f4cf3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711420} {:answer/id #uuid "775c72e0-ac1b-5567-82bc-262bb276abe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711422} {:answer/id #uuid "ca381c20-70db-5915-8fec-c374da3f5205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x}{3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711424} {:answer/id #uuid "d50e61a4-cdcf-5e5a-985d-2ad1953cffb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "775c72e0-ac1b-5567-82bc-262bb276abe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711422} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d13330-e2a4-507f-aaba-2765811f7459" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "440287a6-5183-5d8a-9a73-2790dad1b39d" :question/problem "Given that $3^{y} - y-(2 x^{2})=0$, calculate $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both sides with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a function $y(x)$. The exponential chain rule gives $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(3^{y})=3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(3^{y} - y\\right)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(2 x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}-1\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=4 x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollect the terms containing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$, factor, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1\\right)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=4 x\\\\\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{4 x}{3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis formula applies on real branches where $3^{y} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 1\\ne 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a341603a-c304-527e-9c00-1fc2c30a2f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a341603a-c304-527e-9c00-1fc2c30a2f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711761} :answer-field/id #uuid "a63034f2-40d4-5ba3-92f2-cada017235ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f773cf4c-b595-58c0-89e5-8d179f4c78bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{55}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f773cf4c-b595-58c0-89e5-8d179f4c78bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{55}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711769} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe3b332-ed7b-519b-ac24-d46a196077a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "07d19f85-ed3a-50c5-8b62-238126ec6a2c" :question/problem "The curve has equation $4 x^{2} + 6 x + 2 y^{2} + 2 y=42$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-3,-4\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nGive exact values.\n\n$P=(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8 x + 6+\\left(4 y + 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(4 y + 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(8 x + 6\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{8 x + 6}{4 y + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-18}{-14}=- \\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=- \\frac{9}{7}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=- \\frac{9}{7}\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=- \\frac{9}{7}\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=- \\frac{9}{7}\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(-3\\right)&=-\\frac{-4}{- \\frac{9}{7}} \\\\\nx&=- \\frac{55}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(- \\frac{55}{9},0\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d72adca6-364a-505e-a238-7aa54347ecb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d72adca6-364a-505e-a238-7aa54347ecb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711766} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cccf99-777d-5077-aaa7-ba4d81bba0be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fba4a47-ad1e-54dc-9b03-e819f53889a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fba4a47-ad1e-54dc-9b03-e819f53889a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711760} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c26a330-2e84-57bc-aa6d-4768adb28a7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ac998c8-fae3-5210-9e4f-7eefbd0ac716" :question/problem "The curve has equation $x^{2} + 4 x - 4 y=25$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(3,-1\\right)$ meets the $y$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nGive exact values.\n\n$P=(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 x + 4+\\left(-4\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(-4\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(2 x + 4\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{2 x + 4}{-4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{10}{-4}=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=\\frac{5}{2}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-1\\right)&=\\frac{5}{2}\\left(x-\\left(3\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=\\frac{5}{2}\\left(x-\\left(3\\right)\\right)+\\left(-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\frac{5}{2}\\left(0-\\left(3\\right)\\right)+\\left(-1\\right) \\\\\ny&=- \\frac{17}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(0,- \\frac{17}{2}\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd512c8c-3a59-55d9-9738-64db6ce633e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd512c8c-3a59-55d9-9738-64db6ce633e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711764} :answer-field/id #uuid "135b8999-ef91-5254-8633-294c44542cfa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffe9129-5055-5a76-bfa6-e52efa93e56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffe9129-5055-5a76-bfa6-e52efa93e56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711765} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e42bdb8-ecde-58d7-9aef-fb8b1db9a20b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "37807713-0849-5381-a204-92156855fd76" :question/problem "The curve has equation $x^{2} + 2 y^{2}=24$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-4,-2\\right)$ meets the $y$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nGive exact values.\n\n$P=(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 x+\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(2 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{2 x}{4 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-8}{-8}=-1\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=-1$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-2\\right)&=-1\\left(x-\\left(-4\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=-1\\left(x-\\left(-4\\right)\\right)+\\left(-2\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-1\\left(0-\\left(-4\\right)\\right)+\\left(-2\\right) \\\\\ny&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(0,-6\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e318e43-8b49-5ae9-b8aa-f572e37f7d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e318e43-8b49-5ae9-b8aa-f572e37f7d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711755} :answer-field/id #uuid "0625ec5f-3893-5702-9c0b-28d674e32269" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "513969df-d697-5a16-b6cb-6481dc5d66a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "513969df-d697-5a16-b6cb-6481dc5d66a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711756} :answer-field/id #uuid "20525deb-7187-5d62-8b75-12aac217d8b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5f206418-bfe7-597c-90c6-24fae65ac9d7" :question/problem "The curve has equation $x y + x - 2 y=8$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-4,-2\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nGive exact values.\n\n$P=(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The product rule gives $\\frac{d}{dx}(xy)=y+x\\frac{dy}{dx}$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny + 1+\\left(x - 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(x - 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(y + 1\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{y + 1}{x - 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-1}{-6}=- \\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=- \\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-2\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{6}\\left(x-\\left(-4\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=- \\frac{1}{6}\\left(x-\\left(-4\\right)\\right)+\\left(-2\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=- \\frac{1}{6}\\left(x-\\left(-4\\right)\\right)+\\left(-2\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(-4\\right)&=-\\frac{-2}{- \\frac{1}{6}} \\\\\nx&=-16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(-16,0\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fded8d53-668c-5c7d-8428-e8a04eef14a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fded8d53-668c-5c7d-8428-e8a04eef14a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711770} :answer-field/id #uuid "0981fa9a-8439-5d53-ab71-e3c62873ff9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aea4db8-89ee-5f17-aa70-00692d78b2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1aea4db8-89ee-5f17-aa70-00692d78b2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711751} :answer-field/id #uuid "e06a19f6-86b9-5e6e-a05e-2d854263a638" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1e1cc0e-3255-5a76-8f84-30fa2b0d5757" :question/problem "The curve has equation $x y + 2 x + 2 y=14$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(1,4\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nGive exact values.\n\n$P=(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. The product rule gives $\\frac{d}{dx}(xy)=y+x\\frac{dy}{dx}$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny + 2+\\left(x + 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(x + 2\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(y + 2\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{y + 2}{x + 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{6}{3}=-2\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=-2$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(4\\right)&=-2\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=-2\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)+\\left(4\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=-2\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)+\\left(4\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(1\\right)&=-\\frac{4}{-2} \\\\\nx&=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(3,0\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e88f82e-413d-5bf3-a612-a456953fdb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711791} {:answer/id #uuid "179222a4-7eb7-519f-979b-c080f3623d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,5\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711792} {:answer/id #uuid "5138b472-d843-5943-98f3-45656091f4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,-7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711800} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3f0751-fef5-5c1a-a7fe-39d3efb9fe2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,-9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711804} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbbae01-288f-5db5-bdf2-6bbf1715c641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbbbae01-288f-5db5-bdf2-6bbf1715c641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,9\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711815} :answer-field/id #uuid "63324d57-7db7-588a-a7b9-b5d943ebf408" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b87b4aa-91d2-54c2-88bf-5d19ba04843f" :question/problem "The curve has equation $4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2}=18$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-2,1\\right)$ meets the $y$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $y$-axis, $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8 x+\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(8 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{8 x}{4 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-16}{4}=4\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=4$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(1\\right)&=4\\left(x-\\left(-2\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=4\\left(x-\\left(-2\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=4\\left(0-\\left(-2\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right) \\\\\ny&=9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(0,9\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3372202b-838a-5255-84d9-63aae8209c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(34,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711798} {:answer/id #uuid "7c138b7b-685f-511e-b4c0-25448f4e9018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(16,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711802} {:answer/id #uuid "d08e6575-026b-50e8-9219-4a9e42e26f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-18,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711808} {:answer/id #uuid "d6eb88ed-b0b1-54f8-bdb0-334bb25ddcc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(18,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711809} {:answer/id #uuid "f66eb5cd-8e7f-5fff-aa3c-3bb9cc314db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-14,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6eb88ed-b0b1-54f8-bdb0-334bb25ddcc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(18,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711809} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba7fe66a-d124-5e4c-8af3-590f72631620" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "46873e73-7f1a-5df2-b6ff-b1662bed6345" :question/problem "The curve has equation $2 x^{2} + 4 y^{2}=72$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(2,-4\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $x$-axis, $y=0$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4 x+\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{4 x}{8 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{8}{-32}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=\\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(2\\right)&=-\\frac{-4}{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\\nx&=18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(18,0\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c009f54-3950-5e82-8fba-a30f6210a228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,- \\frac{17}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711790} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd3ed83-43e4-5725-9e99-29cae0c70d16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,-20\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711793} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3227a7-748e-5765-a738-f0fb588e2b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,- \\frac{33}{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711795} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a0bf71-9473-524c-908e-0cf8b8bc87a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,- \\frac{9}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711806} {:answer/id #uuid "eb34ae47-777c-5cd0-b2bd-c2945bc1c0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,- \\frac{15}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c009f54-3950-5e82-8fba-a30f6210a228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,- \\frac{17}{4}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711790} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d9d4474-421f-5045-b851-55b7c4b89d65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e33e57f9-3a10-5c9b-8583-46f871a49199" :question/problem "The curve has equation $x^{2} + 4 y^{2}=68$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(2,-4\\right)$ meets the $y$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $y$-axis, $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 x+\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(2 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{2 x}{8 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{4}{-32}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=\\frac{1}{8}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=\\frac{1}{8}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=\\frac{1}{8}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\frac{1}{8}\\left(0-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right) \\\\\ny&=- \\frac{17}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(0,- \\frac{17}{4}\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186711812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ac7154-3af4-5da0-b744-b2add2096250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{10}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711788} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0e4c48-fe7f-54fb-b7af-b519d97e6839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{8}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711797} {:answer/id #uuid "92d966d2-c9bc-5d9e-a02c-cde2ff3c9206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711803} {:answer/id #uuid "b5636293-1e8e-57c9-899e-cb16788db807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{10}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711805} {:answer/id #uuid "e72e56d4-7884-5068-9e07-ee9f8ab549f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{11}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5636293-1e8e-57c9-899e-cb16788db807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{10}{3},0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711805} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d74d54c-1203-5dd9-b489-ac07d2f7e4d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186711794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9a24671-13ea-533a-9f1e-5df01a4e9266" :question/problem "The curve has equation $3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}=30$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-3,1\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $x$-axis, $y=0$." :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6 x+\\left(6 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(6 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(6 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{6 x}{6 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-18}{6}=3\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=3$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(1\\right)&=3\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=3\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=3\\left(x-\\left(-3\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(-3\\right)&=-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\\nx&=- \\frac{10}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(- \\frac{10}{3},0\\right)$."}]}
